1
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:04,458
[suspenseful music]

2
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:10,375
[as Master Wu]
Focus your Spinjitzu, Arin.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,333
Yes, Master Wu.

4
00:00:12,417 --> 00:00:14,625
[Arin yelling and grunting]

5
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:18,917
Aw, did that hurt, "Ninja nerd"?

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,250
I thought Ninja are
supposed to be tough.

7
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:27,250
Oh, wait, maybe it's because
you're not a Ninja, loser.

8
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:29,000
Careful.

9
00:00:29,083 --> 00:00:32,333
I-I'm fully trained... well,
partially fully trained,

10
00:00:32,417 --> 00:00:34,542
but my mom says I'm
getting way good.

11
00:00:34,625 --> 00:00:38,167
[laughs] Who trained you?

12
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:40,708
Mr. Mop Master here?

13
00:00:43,125 --> 00:00:46,292
-[Arin grunting]
-Who cares about Ninja anyway?

14
00:00:46,375 --> 00:00:49,167
Just a bunch of
babies in pajamas.

15
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:51,750
You better not be
making fun of the Ninja.

16
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:53,625
[dramatic music]

17
00:00:53,708 --> 00:00:56,625
This has nothing to do
with you, Snake Boy.

18
00:00:56,708 --> 00:00:59,958
The Ninja don't sit back when
someone's getting bullied,

19
00:01:00,042 --> 00:01:01,875
and neither do I.

20
00:01:01,958 --> 00:01:04,958
[dramatic music]

21
00:01:05,917 --> 00:01:08,000
[Frak hissing]

22
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:11,042
I probably could
have handled them,

23
00:01:11,125 --> 00:01:12,875
but thanks for the help.

24
00:01:12,958 --> 00:01:14,542
I'm Arin, by the way.

25
00:01:14,625 --> 00:01:15,875
Name's Frak.

26
00:01:15,958 --> 00:01:17,958
You, uh, make that yourself?

27
00:01:18,042 --> 00:01:21,042
Yeah, kind of dorky, right?

28
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:23,875
Better than mine.
I made it outta my
uncle's shed skin,

29
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:25,875
which is kind of gross, I guess,

30
00:01:25,958 --> 00:01:28,792
but I love Master Wu
and the Ninja.

31
00:01:28,875 --> 00:01:30,542
Oh, no way!

32
00:01:30,625 --> 00:01:33,000
Ninja, go!

33
00:01:33,083 --> 00:01:36,500
Lloyd is my favorite,
though I did get a
Zane haircut once.

34
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:39,792
I've always been a Cole guy.
[imitating blast-off]

35
00:01:39,875 --> 00:01:43,458
My dream is to get an Elemental
Power, just like the Ninja.

36
00:01:43,542 --> 00:01:45,458
Oh, wouldn't that be the best?

37
00:01:45,542 --> 00:01:47,167
I'm trying to learn
Spinjitzu on my own

38
00:01:47,250 --> 00:01:51,000
and it's going great,
but also it's going awful.

39
00:01:51,083 --> 00:01:53,250
My parents keep telling me
it's only a matter of time

40
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:56,292
before I'll do a perfect
Spinjitzu tornado.

41
00:01:56,375 --> 00:01:58,208
Oh, I'll practice with you.

42
00:01:58,292 --> 00:02:01,083
[uplifting music]

43
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,958
Arin, what are you doing here?

44
00:02:07,042 --> 00:02:09,833
Right now, being hauled
off by security bots.

45
00:02:09,917 --> 00:02:12,833
I'm here with my master
and these are my guests.

46
00:02:12,917 --> 00:02:14,625
[robot chattering]

47
00:02:14,708 --> 00:02:17,458
[dramatic music]

48
00:02:18,792 --> 00:02:22,292
You're competing in the
Tournament of the Sources?

49
00:02:22,375 --> 00:02:26,750
That's right.
You're looking at the
Elemental Master of Quake!

50
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:30,042
[earthquake rumbling]

51
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:35,250
♪ Lost in the unknown
So much to see ♪

52
00:02:35,333 --> 00:02:37,625
♪ Together we will rise ♪

53
00:02:37,708 --> 00:02:41,292
♪ We fight ♪

54
00:02:41,375 --> 00:02:45,625
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

55
00:02:45,708 --> 00:02:47,375
[fire rumbling]

56
00:02:47,458 --> 00:02:50,667
[earthquake rumbling]

57
00:02:52,167 --> 00:02:55,917
You have Elemental Powers now?
How?

58
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,917
Your mom or dad weren't
masters, were they?

59
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,125
Nope, I was just a regular kid.

60
00:03:01,208 --> 00:03:03,083
But then the Merge
happened, and boom,

61
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:04,792
I could cause things to shake.

62
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:07,500
The first time was so freaky.
I burst a sewer pipe,

63
00:03:07,583 --> 00:03:09,542
which led to a kind of
involved cleanup process

64
00:03:09,625 --> 00:03:12,750
that's probably best
we don't talk about.

65
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:15,083
[dragon chattering]

66
00:03:15,417 --> 00:03:16,875
But then I found a master
who trained me

67
00:03:16,958 --> 00:03:19,000
to use my powers properly.

68
00:03:19,083 --> 00:03:20,542
Why are you here?

69
00:03:20,625 --> 00:03:23,000
You're not gonna
believe this, but--

70
00:03:23,083 --> 00:03:25,500
Arin, Riyu, there you are.

71
00:03:25,583 --> 00:03:27,167
We were so worried.

72
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:31,083
You're here with the Ninja?

73
00:03:31,167 --> 00:03:33,417
I told you
you wouldn't believe it.

74
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:37,333
Hey, everyone.
This is my old friend, Frak.

75
00:03:37,417 --> 00:03:38,708
You mean Frak Frak?

76
00:03:38,792 --> 00:03:40,625
Like the guy who taught
you how to make pies?

77
00:03:40,708 --> 00:03:42,583
If that's true,
we have to thank you.

78
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:45,292
I'm normally a cake guy,
but even I have to admit,

79
00:03:45,375 --> 00:03:47,750
Arin's pies are the best.

80
00:03:47,833 --> 00:03:51,708
The Cole likes my
pie recipes? [laughs]

81
00:03:53,042 --> 00:03:55,250
It's okay, Frak.

82
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:56,750
You wanna come hang out with us?

83
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:58,542
Oh, are you serious?

84
00:03:58,625 --> 00:04:01,083
-I...
-[phone buzzing]

85
00:04:01,167 --> 00:04:04,417
Oh, wait, my master just
sent a training alert.

86
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,417
He does not like
anyone to be late.

87
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:09,208
I gotta run.
I'll find you later, Arin.

88
00:04:09,292 --> 00:04:11,208
It's so amazing to meet you all.

89
00:04:11,292 --> 00:04:13,083
Pleasure to meet you too, Frak.

90
00:04:13,917 --> 00:04:16,500
Nya knows my name.
[stunned shiver]

91
00:04:19,042 --> 00:04:21,375
Arin, we're now officially
invited to the games,

92
00:04:21,458 --> 00:04:22,708
so we're getting a tour.

93
00:04:22,792 --> 00:04:25,083
This is Roby, Master
of Ceremonies,

94
00:04:25,167 --> 00:04:28,750
and his Uncle Bleckt,
the Minister of Ledgering.

95
00:04:28,833 --> 00:04:30,333
Did I get that right?

96
00:04:30,417 --> 00:04:33,292
-Welcome to the--
-Try Minister of Boring.

97
00:04:33,375 --> 00:04:34,833
Ha, I kid, we're family.

98
00:04:34,917 --> 00:04:36,708
He loves it, now come on.

99
00:04:39,125 --> 00:04:42,042
Behold, Foundation Street,

100
00:04:42,125 --> 00:04:44,167
the traditional
center of the city.

101
00:04:44,250 --> 00:04:46,958
[crowd applauding]

102
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,875
This tour is a chance
to keep an eye out

103
00:04:52,958 --> 00:04:54,417
for anyone suspicious.

104
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,583
Remember the real
reason we're here,

105
00:04:56,667 --> 00:04:58,583
to find out who
killed the Matriarch.

106
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:01,958
On it.
Using my keen detective skills.

107
00:05:03,125 --> 00:05:04,625
[Bleckt] Observe the arrangement

108
00:05:04,708 --> 00:05:07,083
of architectural
features as the--

109
00:05:07,167 --> 00:05:09,917
Arrangement of blah, blah, blah.

110
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:13,250
Sorry, Uncle, but is your plan
to put the Ninja to sleep?

111
00:05:14,708 --> 00:05:19,667
The City of Temples must be
treated with reverent respect.

112
00:05:19,750 --> 00:05:21,042
Forget the old rules, Uncs.

113
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:22,583
It's a new era.

114
00:05:22,667 --> 00:05:24,667
The realms are merged.

115
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,708
These are the first
games where I'm in charge

116
00:05:26,792 --> 00:05:29,458
and tradition is out.

117
00:05:29,542 --> 00:05:31,250
It's time for disruption.

118
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:33,375
Ninja, saddle up.

119
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,917
I'm about to show you the
tightest thing in the city.

120
00:05:36,625 --> 00:05:40,833
Check it, seven-headed dragon!

121
00:05:40,917 --> 00:05:42,500
[makes animated noises]

122
00:05:42,583 --> 00:05:43,667
Sweet, right?

123
00:05:43,750 --> 00:05:45,875
Yes, all the yeses!

124
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:48,792
[giggling]

125
00:05:48,875 --> 00:05:50,625
See, she gets it.

126
00:05:50,708 --> 00:05:52,667
She's clearly the smartest one.

127
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:55,000
I have no record of
a seven-headed dragon

128
00:05:55,083 --> 00:05:57,958
in the history of any realm
with which I am acquainted.

129
00:05:58,042 --> 00:06:00,292
That's 'cause it's not real.

130
00:06:00,375 --> 00:06:02,083
It's interpretive
art representing

131
00:06:02,167 --> 00:06:04,833
the Seven Source Dragons of
myth, if you believe in that.

132
00:06:04,917 --> 00:06:06,708
But it's also awesome,

133
00:06:06,792 --> 00:06:08,542
and it's been here,
like, a million years,

134
00:06:08,625 --> 00:06:11,708
so it's almost as
old as Uncle Bleckt. [cackles]

135
00:06:11,792 --> 00:06:14,000
[laughing]

136
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:16,000
Anyhow,
like the fairy tale goes,

137
00:06:16,083 --> 00:06:18,958
all Elemental Powers come
from the Source Dragons.

138
00:06:19,042 --> 00:06:22,083
Is not a fairy tale, Roby.

139
00:06:22,167 --> 00:06:24,500
Whatever. The games were
created forever ago

140
00:06:24,583 --> 00:06:27,125
to celebrate the gifts
of the "Source Dragons."

141
00:06:27,208 --> 00:06:29,875
So Elemental Masters
are called to compete.

142
00:06:29,958 --> 00:06:31,917
It's pretty much a celebration
of your awesomeness.

143
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,375
What does the winner get?

144
00:06:33,458 --> 00:06:35,292
Whoa, we gotta talk rules first.

145
00:06:35,375 --> 00:06:37,042
When someone loses a match,

146
00:06:37,125 --> 00:06:39,333
they give their power
to this Elemental Cup,

147
00:06:39,417 --> 00:06:42,333
and with it, I give their
powers to the winner,

148
00:06:42,417 --> 00:06:44,458
who then has both powers.

149
00:06:44,542 --> 00:06:45,917
Am I right?

150
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,625
This goes on as each
competitor that wins

151
00:06:47,708 --> 00:06:49,625
gains more and more
powers to compete with.

152
00:06:49,708 --> 00:06:52,708
The winner ends up with
everyone's Elemental Powers.

153
00:06:52,792 --> 00:06:55,667
The champion then
returns the Elements

154
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:58,958
to their rightful Masters
in a victory ceremony

155
00:06:59,042 --> 00:07:01,125
that commemorates
the Source Dragons

156
00:07:01,208 --> 00:07:05,292
allowing mortals to be
given Elemental Powers.

157
00:07:05,375 --> 00:07:07,958
Victory ceremonies are boring.

158
00:07:08,042 --> 00:07:11,167
Ours will be an extreme
victory extravaganza.

159
00:07:11,917 --> 00:07:15,083
Doesn't that seem super risky?

160
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:18,083
Yeah, what if the
winner is evil?

161
00:07:18,167 --> 00:07:19,958
They'd have everyone's powers.

162
00:07:20,042 --> 00:07:22,792
They could go rogue and take
over the world or something.

163
00:07:22,875 --> 00:07:24,625
Stop stressing.

164
00:07:24,708 --> 00:07:26,958
Nothing like that's ever
happened, and it couldn't.

165
00:07:27,042 --> 00:07:29,625
The Elemental Cup's
like a safety switch.

166
00:07:29,708 --> 00:07:31,083
Someone tries something stupid,

167
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:33,750
I just pull the powers
back into the Cup,

168
00:07:33,833 --> 00:07:36,708
and only the Games Master, me,

169
00:07:36,792 --> 00:07:38,792
knows the secrets of
how to use this cup.

170
00:07:40,542 --> 00:07:45,500
Lloyd, Arin, what a pleasure
it is to see you old chums.

171
00:07:45,583 --> 00:07:48,458
Zant-Tanz? No way!

172
00:07:48,542 --> 00:07:50,500
This is the guy Arin
and I told you about,

173
00:07:50,583 --> 00:07:52,500
leader of the Mother Garden.

174
00:07:52,583 --> 00:07:55,292
You're an Elemental Master?
Why didn't you tell us?

175
00:07:55,375 --> 00:07:58,417
I didn't even know
until I got invited

176
00:07:58,500 --> 00:08:01,458
to this delightful
convivial convention.

177
00:08:01,542 --> 00:08:03,708
-What's your power?
-Plants.

178
00:08:03,792 --> 00:08:06,375
Witness a whimsical
demonstration.

179
00:08:06,458 --> 00:08:09,375
[air whooshing]

180
00:08:09,458 --> 00:08:12,083
[stones cracking]

181
00:08:12,167 --> 00:08:15,583
[dramatic music]

182
00:08:15,667 --> 00:08:18,292
[laughs] Flower shower.

183
00:08:19,167 --> 00:08:21,417
-Cool.
-Huh, cool.

184
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,500
Oh, I am such a
sucker for whimsy.

185
00:08:23,583 --> 00:08:24,417
Wow.

186
00:08:27,667 --> 00:08:29,958
And you didn't know you
were an Elemental Master?

187
00:08:30,042 --> 00:08:33,708
I just thought I was
very good at gardening.

188
00:08:33,792 --> 00:08:37,417
And I have splendid
news for your tummies.

189
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,083
I'll be bringing my extra
sweet Mucoid Berries

190
00:08:40,167 --> 00:08:41,625
to tonight's banquet.

191
00:08:41,708 --> 00:08:42,917
-Banquet?
-Yep.

192
00:08:43,417 --> 00:08:46,375
Pre-tournament festivities
include dining and delights,

193
00:08:46,458 --> 00:08:48,292
and you're invited, of course.

194
00:08:48,375 --> 00:08:50,458
You'll meet some of
your competitors.

195
00:08:50,542 --> 00:08:53,708
[soft meditative music]

196
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:08,458
Ooh.

197
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:12,667
Oh.

198
00:09:17,667 --> 00:09:19,583
[creature belching]

199
00:09:19,667 --> 00:09:22,208
Ah, here's my favorite team.

200
00:09:22,292 --> 00:09:24,417
Of course, don't tell
anyone else I said that.

201
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:27,000
There's a full buffet,
but also take a menu.

202
00:09:27,083 --> 00:09:29,583
You can order anything
your heart desires.

203
00:09:33,125 --> 00:09:36,417
Come on, let me show you
around this epic banquet.

204
00:09:38,042 --> 00:09:39,625
Tox, is that you?

205
00:09:39,708 --> 00:09:40,875
Like the hair.

206
00:09:40,958 --> 00:09:43,167
Mr. Pale, so good to see you,

207
00:09:43,250 --> 00:09:46,333
uh, not see you. [laughs]

208
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:51,083
[gasps] You!

209
00:09:51,167 --> 00:09:53,083
You disappeared
after the Blood Moon.

210
00:09:53,167 --> 00:09:57,500
-Where'd you--
-[grunts] Help me, Ana.

211
00:09:57,708 --> 00:09:59,000
Huh?

212
00:10:00,458 --> 00:10:02,875
[bones cracking]

213
00:10:02,958 --> 00:10:04,875
Uh, Jordana?

214
00:10:04,958 --> 00:10:08,125
I was wondering where
you got off to, Jordana.

215
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:10,167
[suspenseful music]

216
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,208
I was never far, Nokt.

217
00:10:12,292 --> 00:10:15,000
Look who we have here.

218
00:10:15,583 --> 00:10:19,000
-[Wyldfyre snarling]
-You brought the whole gang?

219
00:10:19,083 --> 00:10:21,917
Hey, didn't you have two
red Ninjas in your group?

220
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,292
I can't remember.

221
00:10:23,375 --> 00:10:24,958
This is for Kai.

222
00:10:25,042 --> 00:10:26,667
Eat fire!

223
00:10:26,750 --> 00:10:29,083
Hold up, hold up, hold up.

224
00:10:29,167 --> 00:10:31,500
No fighting outside the arena.

225
00:10:31,583 --> 00:10:34,667
-Big-time rule.
-But I gotta mess this guy up.

226
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:37,667
Love that energy.
Love it.

227
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:39,583
But save it for the games,

228
00:10:39,667 --> 00:10:42,708
or else, sad face,
you'll be expelled.

229
00:10:42,792 --> 00:10:44,875
Don't blame me.
Just how it is.

230
00:10:46,625 --> 00:10:48,250
Roby's right.

231
00:10:48,333 --> 00:10:50,333
Don't let your anger
get the best of you.

232
00:10:50,417 --> 00:10:52,042
We'll have a chance
to beat them.

233
00:10:52,125 --> 00:10:55,125
[sighs] Okay.

234
00:10:55,208 --> 00:10:56,458
I won't fight.

235
00:10:56,542 --> 00:10:58,583
Want to, but won't.

236
00:10:59,625 --> 00:11:02,542
[dramatic music]

237
00:11:03,417 --> 00:11:04,792
What's wrong, Sora?

238
00:11:04,875 --> 00:11:06,333
Not sure.

239
00:11:06,417 --> 00:11:08,708
Something strange just happened.

240
00:11:08,792 --> 00:11:11,083
[mysterious music]

241
00:11:11,167 --> 00:11:13,167
Wha--

242
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:16,167
Hey, you're a devonian, right?

243
00:11:16,250 --> 00:11:18,208
I've never actually...

244
00:11:18,292 --> 00:11:19,792
Nice to meet you, too.

245
00:11:25,667 --> 00:11:26,667
Ah!

246
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:31,875
-Did I startle you, Lloyd?
-Ras.

247
00:11:31,958 --> 00:11:33,458
If you've come to fight...

248
00:11:33,542 --> 00:11:35,667
We've all come to fight.

249
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:38,625
My team's here to
win the tournament

250
00:11:38,708 --> 00:11:42,250
-and honor the Source Dragons.
-[bell ringing]

251
00:11:42,333 --> 00:11:43,875
[Roby] Ting-ting, ding-ding,
ding-ding, ting-ting.

252
00:11:43,958 --> 00:11:45,167
Hi, hi.

253
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:47,625
Attention, Masters.

254
00:11:47,708 --> 00:11:51,917
One night before the New
Tournament of the Sources,

255
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,167
I am reminded of what
the Cragling poet,

256
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:57,042
Rockworth, once said.

257
00:11:57,792 --> 00:12:01,375
[growling, rock-grinding noises]

258
00:12:04,792 --> 00:12:07,375
I have been betrayed
for the last time.

259
00:12:07,458 --> 00:12:08,833
[guests gasping]

260
00:12:08,917 --> 00:12:10,750
Empress Beatrix?

261
00:12:14,667 --> 00:12:16,833
[robots chattering]

262
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:21,500
We've beaten you once,
Empress, and we'll do it again.

263
00:12:21,583 --> 00:12:22,875
Empress?

264
00:12:23,583 --> 00:12:28,500
[chuckles] So you must be the
Ninja who dethroned my sister.

265
00:12:28,583 --> 00:12:30,292
You had no right.

266
00:12:30,375 --> 00:12:32,875
I spent years plotting
my revenge on my twin,

267
00:12:32,958 --> 00:12:34,958
and you stole that from me.

268
00:12:35,042 --> 00:12:36,417
Twin?

269
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:39,083
-You're--
-Zeatrix!

270
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:41,667
Yeah, don't love
you storming in.

271
00:12:41,750 --> 00:12:44,167
All your sloppy drama's
messing up my big speech.

272
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:47,875
A banquet to which the
Elemental Master of Shockwave

273
00:12:47,958 --> 00:12:50,792
was not invited is
a grave act of betrayal

274
00:12:50,875 --> 00:12:53,208
-I will not forgive.
-Ugh.

275
00:12:53,292 --> 00:12:55,875
Everything with you is
grave act to betrayal this,

276
00:12:55,958 --> 00:12:57,833
a pox upon your house that.

277
00:12:57,917 --> 00:13:00,083
I'm sure not inviting you
was just an oversight,

278
00:13:00,167 --> 00:13:01,417
right, Uncle Bleckt?

279
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,833
[suspenseful music]

280
00:13:03,917 --> 00:13:05,208
Oversight?

281
00:13:05,292 --> 00:13:07,167
I still haven't been
assigned quarters

282
00:13:07,250 --> 00:13:09,375
like every other competitor,

283
00:13:09,458 --> 00:13:12,125
and now I'm excluded
from the welcome banquet?

284
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,542
I know what you're doing.

285
00:13:13,625 --> 00:13:15,292
You're sidelining
me because you know

286
00:13:15,375 --> 00:13:18,625
I'm destined to destroy
every single one of these

287
00:13:18,708 --> 00:13:21,042
so-called masters in the games.

288
00:13:21,125 --> 00:13:23,833
-[laughs] All right.
-[laughs] Yeah, right.

289
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:29,958
Your sister didn't find you
so difficult to defeat.

290
00:13:30,875 --> 00:13:34,083
-[gasps]
-Ras! [snarls]

291
00:13:36,458 --> 00:13:40,625
What are you doing here?
You're no Elemental Master.

292
00:13:41,583 --> 00:13:44,750
I command Elemental Masters.

293
00:13:45,792 --> 00:13:48,708
I know you conspired
with my sister

294
00:13:48,792 --> 00:13:51,375
to take my father's life.

295
00:13:51,458 --> 00:13:55,500
I look forward to you
meeting the same fate.

296
00:13:55,583 --> 00:13:57,417
[Ras growling]

297
00:13:58,042 --> 00:14:02,208
Roby, any more oversights,
and you will pay, personally.

298
00:14:04,125 --> 00:14:09,125
Zeatrix, Elemental Master
of Buzzkill, am I right?

299
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:12,292
Dude, my speech
was gonna be epic.

300
00:14:12,375 --> 00:14:15,875
But the moment's gone.
Everyone eat, eat.

301
00:14:15,958 --> 00:14:17,875
Game's tomorrow, whatever.

302
00:14:21,958 --> 00:14:24,000
[Nya] I've been to some
awkward dinners,

303
00:14:24,083 --> 00:14:25,875
like when Jay ate
the host's fern

304
00:14:25,958 --> 00:14:27,792
thinking it was a side salad.

305
00:14:27,875 --> 00:14:29,417
Or when Jay asked for
sushi from a fish waiter

306
00:14:29,500 --> 00:14:31,250
in the undersea
kingdom of Merlopia.

307
00:14:32,958 --> 00:14:34,875
Actually, being with Jay
led to many awkward dinners.

308
00:14:34,958 --> 00:14:37,917
But tonight was in the top ten.

309
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,417
I thought I was seeing
Beatrix in my visions

310
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:41,875
this whole time.

311
00:14:41,958 --> 00:14:43,875
But was it Zeatrix?

312
00:14:43,958 --> 00:14:45,542
What could it mean?

313
00:14:45,625 --> 00:14:47,875
Maybe it means she's the
one who killed the Matriarch

314
00:14:47,958 --> 00:14:49,167
and took her horns.

315
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:50,625
What makes you think that?

316
00:14:50,708 --> 00:14:52,875
We know the horns are
a source of power.

317
00:14:52,958 --> 00:14:55,875
What if she plans to use them
somehow to win the games?

318
00:14:55,958 --> 00:14:58,000
She seemed pretty
confident she'd win,

319
00:14:58,083 --> 00:15:00,625
like she knows something
that the rest of us don't.

320
00:15:01,375 --> 00:15:02,875
It's gotta be Ras.

321
00:15:02,958 --> 00:15:04,875
He's attacked the
Matriarch before,

322
00:15:04,958 --> 00:15:06,750
and he captured a Source Dragon.

323
00:15:06,833 --> 00:15:08,875
And Ras did the whole
Blood Moon thing

324
00:15:08,958 --> 00:15:12,167
because he wanted to bring
back the Forbidden Five.

325
00:15:12,250 --> 00:15:14,417
What if it was for these games?

326
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,750
And when he didn't get all five,

327
00:15:15,833 --> 00:15:18,417
maybe he needed the
horns as a backup plan.

328
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:21,125
The winner does get
everyone's Elemental Powers.

329
00:15:21,208 --> 00:15:24,292
That kind of thing
smells like a Ras plan

330
00:15:24,375 --> 00:15:27,000
and ties it all to
the Source Dragons.

331
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,000
Crazy dinner.

332
00:15:29,083 --> 00:15:31,542
But it's obvious who
the dragon killer is.

333
00:15:33,917 --> 00:15:35,917
Right, Ras.

334
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,208
Or Zeatrix.

335
00:15:38,417 --> 00:15:41,625
What?
No, it's definitely Bleckt.

336
00:15:42,542 --> 00:15:44,333
The stuffy ledger guy?

337
00:15:44,417 --> 00:15:47,708
You've seen how he
treats the amazing Roby.

338
00:15:47,792 --> 00:15:50,042
[scoffs] Jealous much?

339
00:15:50,125 --> 00:15:53,292
"The amazing Roby"?

340
00:15:53,375 --> 00:15:55,917
All of these theories
are worth considering,

341
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,667
but we do not have enough
data to reach a conclusion.

342
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:01,375
Zane's right, we
need to know more.

343
00:16:01,458 --> 00:16:04,417
Rest up.
The games start tomorrow.

344
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:07,375
[mysterious music]

345
00:16:10,917 --> 00:16:13,583
[dragon yawning]

346
00:16:17,125 --> 00:16:18,875
[sighs]

347
00:16:20,458 --> 00:16:21,875
[crickets chirping]

348
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:25,875
[Ninjas snoring]

349
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:29,750
[suspenseful music]

350
00:16:34,042 --> 00:16:37,583
[dragon grumbling]

351
00:16:40,917 --> 00:16:43,750
[dragon roaring]

352
00:16:45,792 --> 00:16:47,042
What's going on?

353
00:16:47,958 --> 00:16:49,417
[Zane] It is an armed intruder.

354
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:51,833
Detecting high
levels of hostility.

355
00:16:52,833 --> 00:16:56,333
You tried to Ninja into
a room full of Ninja?

356
00:16:56,417 --> 00:16:58,083
Not smart, buddy.

357
00:16:58,167 --> 00:17:00,042
[dragon roaring]

358
00:17:00,125 --> 00:17:02,792
[dramatic music]

359
00:17:08,917 --> 00:17:11,792
[powers rumbling]

360
00:17:14,750 --> 00:17:16,375
[window crashing]

361
00:17:24,583 --> 00:17:27,917
No one sneaks into--
Hey! [grunts]

362
00:17:34,875 --> 00:17:37,250
[dragon roaring]

363
00:17:39,167 --> 00:17:41,625
I was actually getting a good
night's sleep for a change.

364
00:17:41,708 --> 00:17:43,208
Thanks for ruining that.

365
00:17:44,917 --> 00:17:46,958
[air whooshing]

366
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,167
Who are you?
Did Ras send you?

367
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:58,833
[air whooshing]

368
00:17:58,917 --> 00:18:02,125
[grunting]

369
00:18:06,417 --> 00:18:08,542
Oh, we're not done talking.

370
00:18:12,125 --> 00:18:14,167
[wood crashing]

371
00:18:14,542 --> 00:18:17,750
[grunting]

372
00:18:20,917 --> 00:18:22,750
[wood crashing]

373
00:18:22,833 --> 00:18:25,292
[dramatic music]

374
00:18:28,917 --> 00:18:30,083
[dogs bark]

375
00:18:31,375 --> 00:18:32,458
[sighs]

376
00:18:36,667 --> 00:18:39,833
Stop.
You are disturbing the peace.

377
00:18:39,917 --> 00:18:43,042
Conflict is only allowed
during the games.

378
00:18:44,917 --> 00:18:46,833
Lloyd, is that you?

379
00:18:46,917 --> 00:18:49,208
What's all this
hubbub and commotion?

380
00:18:49,292 --> 00:18:50,833
Whoever this is
just tried to give me

381
00:18:50,917 --> 00:18:53,250
an early wake-up call with this.

382
00:18:54,167 --> 00:18:56,833
-[crowd gasping]
-It is true.

383
00:18:56,917 --> 00:18:58,542
We are all witnesses.

384
00:18:58,625 --> 00:18:59,917
Who is it, Lloyd?

385
00:19:00,667 --> 00:19:01,792
Let's find out.

386
00:19:03,125 --> 00:19:04,417
A bot?

387
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:07,458
[electricity crackling]

388
00:19:09,750 --> 00:19:12,000
That's definitely not
one of our security bots,

389
00:19:12,083 --> 00:19:13,708
I can tell you that.

390
00:19:13,792 --> 00:19:15,917
Whatever it is, I have
a pretty good guess

391
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,292
about who sent it.

392
00:19:18,625 --> 00:19:22,917
Do you? Maybe it's the same
person who sent one after me.

393
00:19:23,917 --> 00:19:26,167
[bot crashing]

394
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,125
And a third
attacker, it appears.

395
00:19:31,792 --> 00:19:33,625
The damage is too extensive

396
00:19:33,708 --> 00:19:36,000
to access its mechanical memory.

397
00:19:36,083 --> 00:19:38,208
Then how can we
know who sent them?

398
00:19:40,875 --> 00:19:43,792
Tox, you're the Elemental
Master of Poison.

399
00:19:43,875 --> 00:19:45,042
What do you make of this?

400
00:19:46,708 --> 00:19:48,792
Hmm, no question.

401
00:19:48,875 --> 00:19:52,000
That's a rare Gelba thorn
from the Sevateam plant.

402
00:19:52,083 --> 00:19:54,083
Never heard of it.
Where are they from?

403
00:19:54,167 --> 00:19:58,958
Only one place in all the
Merged Lands, the Mother Garden.

404
00:19:59,042 --> 00:20:00,667
But the Mother
Garden's protected.

405
00:20:00,750 --> 00:20:02,208
You can't take
plants outta there

406
00:20:02,292 --> 00:20:05,500
without the permission
of its leader.

407
00:20:06,875 --> 00:20:10,833
Well, yes, I am the general
of the Mucoid Warriors

408
00:20:10,917 --> 00:20:13,583
and supreme leader
of the Mother Garden,

409
00:20:13,667 --> 00:20:17,458
but I assure you, I've got
nothing to do with this.

410
00:20:18,333 --> 00:20:20,833
Although, Tox is correct about

411
00:20:20,917 --> 00:20:23,583
the origin of the Gelba thorns.

412
00:20:23,667 --> 00:20:25,875
They can only come from my home.

413
00:20:25,958 --> 00:20:28,292
[crowd gasping]

414
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:32,583
Zant-Tanz is our friend.
I'm sure he didn't do this.

415
00:20:33,292 --> 00:20:36,333
He is not my friend.

416
00:20:37,292 --> 00:20:39,833
The thorns prove
it can only be him.

417
00:20:39,917 --> 00:20:42,333
And attacking fellow
competitors is penalized

418
00:20:42,417 --> 00:20:43,792
with immediate exile.

419
00:20:45,208 --> 00:20:47,833
I'm telling you, there's
no way Zant-Tanz--

420
00:20:47,917 --> 00:20:49,333
I want him gone.

421
00:20:49,542 --> 00:20:51,667
[crowd muttering]

422
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,542
Looks like you're
not the only one.

423
00:20:53,625 --> 00:20:54,958
But it's not fair.

424
00:20:55,042 --> 00:20:56,833
Lloyd, it's okay.

425
00:20:56,917 --> 00:20:58,625
I'm innocent.

426
00:20:58,708 --> 00:21:00,833
But if my leaving
would comfort people,

427
00:21:00,917 --> 00:21:04,667
I will exile myself voluntarily.

428
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:07,958
I do have some rock-stacking
to do at home.

429
00:21:08,042 --> 00:21:12,625
However, be warned,
I did not do this.

430
00:21:12,708 --> 00:21:16,125
Whoever sent these attacker
bots is still among you.

431
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,375
Sure, sure, whatever.
[fingers snapping]

432
00:21:24,833 --> 00:21:26,750
Enough excitement for one night.

433
00:21:26,833 --> 00:21:28,292
Get some rest, everyone.

434
00:21:28,375 --> 00:21:30,458
First competitions are tomorrow!

435
00:21:32,333 --> 00:21:34,917
Huh?
Jay?

436
00:21:35,917 --> 00:21:38,833
Jay?
Jay!

437
00:21:38,917 --> 00:21:41,750
[mysterious music]

438
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:47,917
[closing theme music plays]

